.TH OTPME 1 "2026-09-18" "OTPme 0.3.0a278" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme \- global options for OTPme management commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme\-\fIname\fR
[\fIglobal options\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
All OTPme management commands (otpme-user, otpme-token, otpme-client, etc.) share a common set of global options described here. For a conceptual overview of the OTPme system, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.SS Connection Options
.TP
.B \-r \fIrealm\fR
Connect to a specific realm.
.TP
.B \-s \fIsite\fR
Connect to a specific site.
.TP
.B \-t \fItimeout\fR
How long to wait until the connection to the daemon is established, in seconds. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-tt \fItimeout\fR
How long to wait when a request is sent and for its answer, in seconds. Default: 15.
Use a higher value for commands that take long on the server.
.TP
.B \-\-reneg\-timeout \fItimeout\fR
Only for \fBotpme\-agent\fR: how long the agent waits for an answer when it renews a login session, in seconds. Default: 30.
.TP
.B \-c \fIconfig_file\fR
Use alternative config file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dns
Do not resolve OTPme site address via DNS.
This is the default, see \fBUSE_DNS\fR in
.BR otpme.conf (5).
.TP
.B \-\-use\-dns
Resolve OTPme site address via DNS.
.TP
.B \-\-login\-no\-dns
Do not resolve OTPme login point via DNS.
.TP
.B \-\-login\-use\-dns
Resolve OTPme login point via DNS.
This is the default, see \fBLOGIN_USE_DNS\fR in
.BR otpme.conf (5).
.SS Authentication Options
.TP
.B \-\-use\-ssh\-agent \fBy\fR|\fBn\fR
Use ssh-agent for authentication (\fBy\fR) or not (\fBn\fR). The value is required.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-smartcard \fBy\fR|\fBn\fR
Use a smartcard for authentication (\fBy\fR) or not (\fBn\fR). The value is required.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-pass
Read the password, OTP or PIN from stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-token \fItoken\fR
Emulate login with given token in API mode.
.TP
.B \-u \fIusername\fR
User used for authentication (e.g. when joining the realm as an ordinary user rather than the local root).
.TP
.B \-\-impersonate\-token \fIuser\fB/\fItoken\fR
Work as the given token, for example \fBalice/login\fR. Needs admin permissions.
You can not impersonate your own token, the token of the realm admin, or a token or user in \fBsite_admin_blacklist\fR.
Each use is written to the log and the audit log.
Has no effect with \fB\-\-api\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-fetch\-scripts
Fetch scripts from the server instead of using cached ones.
.SS Communication Options
.TP
.B \-\-socket
Send the command to mgmtd over its local Unix socket instead of the network.
This only works on a node.
No login is needed: mgmtd takes the name of the local system user and works as the OTPme user of the same name, with that user's default token.
See also \fBUSE_MGMTD_SOCKET\fR in
.BR otpme.conf (5).
.TP
.B \-\-api
Run the command in this process, directly on the local data, without a daemon and without a login.
This only works on a node, normally as root.
Use it with care while the OTPme daemons are running: changes can be lost or break things.
OTPme prints a warning in this case.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-type \fIobject_type\fR
Object type to act on, for example the token type.
It goes before the command, for example \fBotpme\-token \-\-type totp add alice/totp\fR.
.TP
.B \-f
Do not ask any questions: every confirmation counts as answered with yes.
This also applies to deleting objects and to signing:
with \fB\-f\fR, data is signed without showing it to you first.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-pager
Do not page command output through a pager (e.g. \fBless\fR) even when it exceeds the terminal size. See also \fBUSE_PAGER\fR in
.BR otpme.conf (5).
.TP
.B \-\-changelog \fItext\fR
Add the given text as a custom entry to the object changelog written by this command. Only meaningful for commands that change an object.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-raw\-sign\-data
When you are asked to sign something (for example a job of
.BR otpme\-deploy (1)),
show the raw data that is signed instead of the short summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version.
.TP
.B \-v
Enable verbose mode.
.SS Debug Options
Debug options start with \fB\-d\fR, followed by one or more letters.
\fB\-d\fR alone is not valid.
Each letter selects a topic, a letter with a digit a sub topic (for example \fB\-dc\fR for object caching, \fB\-dc1\fR for cache flushing).
You can combine topics in one option, for example \fB\-dcn\fR.
Some topics have levels: repeat the letter to raise the level (\fB\-dee\fR, \fB\-dTT\fR).
.PP
Selecting a topic sets the log level to DEBUG, so its messages are shown.
The options that change how OTPme runs (\fB\-dD\fR, \fB\-de\fR, \fB\-dE\fR, \fB\-dP\fR, \fB\-dt\fR) do not change the log level.
.PP
\fBGeneral\fR
.TP
.B \-dd
Show the log on stdout, at the log level it already has.
Use this to watch a daemon that runs in the foreground (\fB\-dDd\fR) without reading everything it does.
.TP
.B \-ddd
Show the log on stdout at log level DEBUG.
This is everything, and it is a lot.
.TP
.B \-dD
Do not go to background.
On its own it says nothing: add \fB\-dd\fR to see the log, so \fB\-dDd\fR to watch a daemon work and \fB\-dDdd\fR to see everything it does.
.TP
.B \-dt
Add timestamps to debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-color\-logs
Show log messages in color.
.TP
.B \-de
Print tracebacks.
.TP
.B \-dee
Print tracebacks and raise exceptions instead of handling them.
.TP
.B \-dE
Add exception info to warning, error, critical and fatal log messages (sets \fBLOG_EXC_INFO\fR for this run).
.PP
\fBCaches\fR
.TP
.B \-dc
Print when objects are read from cache.
.TP
.B \-dc1
Print when caches are flushed.
.TP
.B \-da
Print when entries are added to function caches.
.TP
.B \-dh
Print function cache hits.
.PP
\fBBackend and files\fR
.TP
.B \-db
Print when objects are read from the backend.
.TP
.B \-dr
Print file reads.
.TP
.B \-dw
Print file writes.
.TP
.B \-dA
Debug transactions.
.TP
.B \-dA1
Debug reading and writing of transactions on disk.
.TP
.B \-dA2
Debug each single transaction action.
.PP
\fBLocks\fR
.TP
.B \-dL
Debug locks.
.TP
.B \-dL1
Debug waiting for locks.
.PP
\fBNetwork and protocols\fR
.TP
.B \-dn
Debug connections (accept, connect, close).
.TP
.B \-dN
Debug network packets.
.TP
.B \-dp
Debug protocol handling (preauth, commands).
.TP
.B \-dC
Debug client messages.
.TP
.B \-dC1
Debug client side crypto (keys, DH, signatures).
.TP
.B \-dH
Debug host authentication (certificates, challenges).
.PP
\fBCluster and sync\fR
.TP
.B \-ds
Debug object sync.
.TP
.B \-dS
Debug cluster communication.
.PP
\fBObjects\fR
.TP
.B \-do
Debug policies.
.TP
.B \-dx
Debug object extensions.
.PP
\fBProcesses and modules\fR
.TP
.B \-df
Debug forking and dropping of privileges.
.TP
.B \-dm
Print when OTPme modules are loaded.
.PP
\fBProfiling and timing\fR
.TP
.B \-dM
Trace function and method calls.
.TP
.B \-dP
Profile with cProfile.
.TP
.B \-dT
Print a warning if a function or method call takes longer than \fB\-\-debug\-timing\-limit\fR.
.TP
.B \-dTT
Print the timing result after each method finishes (instead of the warnings of \fB\-dT\fR).
.TP
.B \-dTTT
Print a warning each time a method call gets slower (instead of the output of \fB\-dT\fR and \fB\-dTT\fR).
.PP
\fBFilters and limits\fR
.TP
.B \-\-log\-filter \fIdaemon1,daemon2\fR
Only show log messages of the given daemons, for example \fBmgmtd,syncd\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-daemons \fIdaemon1,daemon2\fR
Only apply the debug options inside the given daemons.
Commands you run from a shell are not affected.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-users \fIuser1,user2\fR
Only trace and time calls made for requests of the given users.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-func\-names \fIregex1,regex2\fR
With \fB\-dT\fR: only time the functions and methods whose full name (\fImodule.class.method\fR) matches one of the regular expressions.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-func\-start \fIregex1,regex2\fR
With \fB\-dT\fR: start timing at the first call of a function or method that matches one of the regular expressions.
From then on, all calls are timed.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-func\-caches \fIcache1,cache2\fR
With \fB\-da\fR or \fB\-dh\fR: only show the given function caches.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-timing\-limit \fIseconds\fR
With \fB\-dT\fR: warn about calls that take longer than this. The timing results also only show functions whose total time is longer.
Default: 0.2.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-profile\-sort \fBcumtime\fR|\fBncalls\fR|\fBtottime\fR
With \fB\-dP\fR: how the profile output is sorted. Default: \fBtottime\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-profile\-print\-callers \fIfunc1,func2\fR
With \fB\-dP\fR: also show who called the given functions.
.SS Job Options
.TP
.B \-\-lock\-wait\-timeout \fIseconds\fR
How long to wait for an object that another job has locked. Default: 0 (do not wait, fail at once).
.TP
.B \-\-job\-timeout \fIseconds\fR
Stop the job on the server when it shows no activity for this long. Default: 60.
.SS Advanced Options
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-typing
Check on every function call that the arguments have the types the code expects (Python type hints).
This is for finding bugs and makes everything slower.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-locking
Do not lock objects while changing them.
This only has an effect with \fB\-\-api\fR, because normally mgmtd does the locking.
Only use it when nothing else changes objects at the same time: changes can get lost.
.SS Daemon Options
These options are used when starting the daemons with \fBotpme\-controld\fR.
.TP
.B \-l \fIfile\fR
Write the log to this file instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-index\-start
Do not start and stop the index database with the daemons.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache\-start
Do not start and stop the cache with the daemons.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-flush
Empty the cache when the daemons start.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-changed\-objects
hostd syncs objects even if they change while syncing.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-floating\-ip
On the master node: do not remove the floating IP when the daemons stop.
